/*!
\page page_sthlttriggerreason StHltTriggerReason

\brief Associates an HLT trigger reason bit with the specific physics object that fired the online trigger.

\section overview Overview

`StHltTriggerReason` links an HLT trigger bit to the physics object that caused the online trigger
decision. Each event may contain multiple entries if several physics signatures fired. The
`mReasonBit` field identifies the trigger type; the `mReason` link points polymorphically—through
\ref StHltTriggerReasonCapable—to the actual \ref StHltHighPt, \ref StHltDiElectron, or
\ref StHltHeavyFragment object. The aggregate bitmask is in \ref StHltEvent::triggerReasonBitOred.

\subsection trigbits StHltTriggerReasonType Enum

| Enum | Value | Meaning |
|------|-------|---------|
| `kHighPt` | `0x10000` | High-pT track trigger |
| `kDiElectron` | `0x20000` | Di-electron pair trigger |
| `kHeavyFragment` | `0x40000` | Heavy nuclear fragment trigger |
| `kAllEvents` | `0x80000` | Accept-all events |
| `kRandomEvents` | `0x100000` | Random event sampling |
| `kBESGoodEvents` | `0x200000` | BES good-event trigger |

\section hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StHltTriggerReason
\endcode

\section datamembers Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StHltTriggerReasonType` | `mReasonBit` | Trigger reason bit |
| *(StLink)* | `mReason` | Pointer to the triggering \ref StHltTriggerReasonCapable object |

\section keymethods Key Methods

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `StHltTriggerReasonType reasonBit() const` | Returns the trigger reason bit |
| `StHltTriggerReasonCapable* reason() const` | Returns the triggering physics object |

\section example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
for (size_t i = 0; i < hlt->triggerReason().size(); ++i) {
    const StHltTriggerReason* tr = hlt->triggerReason()[i];
    if (tr->reasonBit() == kHighPt) {
        const StHltHighPt* hp = static_cast<const StHltHighPt*>(tr->reason());
        cout << "HighPt pT=" << hp->primaryTrack().pt() << endl;
    }
}
\endcode

\see StHltEvent
\see StHltTriggerReasonCapable
\see StHltHighPt
\see StHltDiElectron
\see StHltHeavyFragment
*/
